The `add_book` method takes a `Book` object as an argument, creates a new node in the tree if there is no root node or the current node has less than 8 children (the maximum depth of the tree), and adds the book to the node. If the current node has more than 7 children, it handles this case as needed by creating new child nodes or moving books to appropriate locations in the tree structure.

The `get_data` method takes a position argument and retrieves the data at that position in the tree. If the root node is not None and there are no child nodes at the specified position, it returns the title and author of the root node. Otherwise, it recursively traverses the child nodes until it finds a leaf node or reaches a maximum depth and returns the title and author of the found node.

